From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 22:56:54 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: beamforming record follows width and
 stream changes

When a station changed width or stream count (an Operating Mode
Notification), mt7915_mac_sta_rc_work() sent only STA_REC_RA and
STA_REC_HE, so STA_REC_BF kept the width, the PFMU memory sized for it
and the column count it got at association. Even sent again, its
columns came from the station's MCS maps alone and wouldn't have
followed a drop in streams.

mt7915_mcu_add_rate_ctrl() now takes the rc work's IEEE80211_RC_*
changes instead of a bool, and on a width or stream change adds
mt7915_mcu_sta_bfer_tlv() first, as when the station is added. That
function decides the same way as there: a station we beamform neither
explicitly nor implicitly (debugfs implicit_txbf) gets no record. HE and
VHT column counts (ncol, ibf_ncol, ncol_gt_bw80) are now also capped at
rx_nss, the streams mac80211 says the station takes now; on 2.4 and
5 GHz that is its map's count until an Operating Mode Notification
lowers it (see the previous commit). HT stations can't send one, so HT
is left as it was.

The firmware already gets STA_REC_BF for a station it has a record of:
at association and again at authorization (both mt7915_mcu_add_sta()).
What's new is a different size for a PFMU it has, which hasn't been
tried on hardware. With beamforming off, no station has a record and
nothing changes.

mt7915_test_add_rate_ctrl_bf checks which changes send STA_REC_BF,
sized for the new width and streams, and that a station without one
gets none; mt7915_test_bfer_nss that columns follow rx_nss for HE at
and above 80 MHz and for VHT explicit and implicit; and
mt7915_test_sta_rc_work_bf the rc work per change. All three fail
without the fix. mt7915_test_bfer_he's 160 MHz station now takes the
three streams its map gives it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
